   "text": {
    "L1": "To add decimals, line up the decimal points first.",
    "L2": "A common mistake is lining up the last digits like whole numbers. That does not keep place values together.",
    "L3": "For 14.6 plus 2.85, write 14.6 as 14.60 so both numbers have hundredths.",
    "L4": "Now the points line up: 14.60 is above 2.85.",
    "L5": "Add the hundredths: zero plus five is five. Then add the tenths: six plus eight is fourteen, so write four and carry one.",
    "L6": "Add the ones: four plus two plus the carried one is seven. The answer is 17.45.",
    "L7": "For subtraction, write a whole number with zeros, such as 5.00, and trade exactly as with whole numbers.",
    "L8": "Estimate with whole numbers to check that your answer makes sense. Now choose the correct sum."
   },
